 "arc": "A club step-touch. It opens on the balls of both feet with the character-left arm held at shoulder height, elbow bent, and the character-right arm out to the side. At frame 1 the weight moves onto the character-right foot and the character-left foot lifts, held through frame 3; it steps back down at frame 4 with a small lean to character-left.\n\nFrom frame 5 the arms drop: character-left through chest height to the waist by frame 6, character-right to the waist by frame 7. From frame 9 the figure centres over both feet, arms settled at the waist, bouncing lightly on the balls of the feet. Pingpong: frames 0 and 14 are the grounded turnarounds; the lifted-foot, arm-up opening is the hit pose.",
